## Complexity Analysis

Where:
- `n` = Initial length of string
- `r` = Number of rounds

| Approach | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
|----------|-----------------|------------------|
| Brute Force | O(n × r) | O(n) |
| Better | O(n × r) | O(n) |
| Optimized | O(n × r) | O(n) |

**Note:** All three approaches use the same simulation algorithm. The second approach uses `join()` for efficient string construction, while the third preserves the original nested-loop solution.

